==================================================
7. IMAGE DELIVERY HARDENING
==================================================

Audit all images for:

- broken paths
- incorrect formats
- missing dimensions
- missing alt text
- incorrect `sizes`
- incorrect priority
- unnecessary eager loading
- unnecessary preload
- oversized source assets
- layout shift risks

Use `next/image` where appropriate.

Preserve the Phase 3.5 hero strategy:

- initial hero image may be prioritized/preloaded
- other hero images remain non-blocking
- below-fold imagery remains lazy where appropriate

Do NOT:

- preload every image
- eagerly load every image
- remove meaningful images
- sacrifice visible quality unnecessarily

==================================================
8. FONT / CSS FINAL HARDENING
==================================================

Verify:

- Plus Jakarta Sans loads correctly
- Cormorant Garamond loads correctly
- no accidental fallback to another design font
- no unnecessary font weights
- no duplicate font declarations
- no external font dependency unless intentionally required

Audit CSS/Tailwind for:

- obsolete classes
- contradictory styles
- accidental gradients
- excessive rounded corners
- hidden overflow that masks layout problems
- unnecessary animations
- duplicated rules

Do not introduce a new styling system.

==================================================
9. JAVASCRIPT / CLIENT COMPONENT AUDIT
==================================================

Review all `"use client"` components.

For each client component determine whether client-side behavior is genuinely required.

Where safe:

- keep static components server-rendered
- reduce unnecessary hydration
- remove unnecessary state
- remove unnecessary effects
- remove unnecessary browser event listeners

Do not perform risky rewrites.

Do not break existing interactive components.

==================================================
10. HYDRATION / RUNTIME ERROR HARDENING
==================================================

Audit for likely hydration problems.

Check for:

- browser APIs during server rendering
- date/time differences
- random values during render
- unstable IDs
- conditional rendering that differs server/client
- client-only data used during SSR
- image dimension mismatches

Run the production application.

Inspect runtime output for:

- hydration errors
- uncaught exceptions
- failed requests
- broken asset requests
- server errors

Fix real issues found.

